Transform or display canonical strap state.

Usage:
  strap state init
  strap state add-user "hello"
  strap state bookmark add --text "unique substring" --label fold-start < state.json > next.json
  strap state bookmark list < state.json
  strap state extract --from bm_a --to bm_b < state.json > context.json
  strap state fold --from bm_a --to bm_b --summary "summary" < state.json > next.json
  strap state locate --text "unique substring" < state.json
  strap state show bm_a < state.json
  strap state tree --hidden < state.json
  strap state display-last-message

The command reads state from stdin for transforms and writes the next state to stdout.
